WEBVTT

00:02.380 --> 00:03.250
Finally...

00:03.830 --> 00:05.380
The long-awaited day is here!

00:06.670 --> 00:07.500
At last...

00:07.880 --> 00:10.000
This Friday is finally the day!

00:11.130 --> 00:12.250
<b>Animovie News</b>

00:11.130 --> 00:12.250
<b>The film adaptation of the popular manga Sword x Magic</b>

00:11.130 --> 00:12.250
<b>begins screening nationwide in April!!</b>

00:12.290 --> 00:14.750
<b>Nationwide</b>

00:12.290 --> 00:14.750
<b>theatrical release</b>

00:12.830 --> 00:13.830
I've waited so long!

00:13.830 --> 00:14.790
Hey!

00:15.000 --> 00:15.830
For this!

00:15.830 --> 00:16.960
Hey!

00:17.540 --> 00:19.540
Hey, Shiraishi-kun!

00:20.210 --> 00:21.790
K..Kubo-san!

00:21.790 --> 00:23.330
You finally noticed.

00:23.880 --> 00:26.670
What's up? You seem like you're in a good mood.

00:26.670 --> 00:28.330
Oh, I do?

00:31.210 --> 00:34.460
So a manga I like got a movie adaptation.

00:34.460 --> 00:37.170
It'll be out soon, and I just can't wait.

00:37.170 --> 00:38.000
A movie?

00:38.540 --> 00:41.460
Kubo-san doesn't seem like
she'd be into movies like that.

00:41.880 --> 00:44.920
Oh! By any chance, is it that manga
that you leant me before?

00:45.920 --> 00:46.750
Yeah.

00:47.630 --> 00:53.080
The manga you leant me was really enjoyable,
so I collected every volume!

00:53.080 --> 00:54.960
What, you did?

00:55.880 --> 00:58.130
Who are you seeing the movie with?

00:59.040 --> 01:00.080
I'm seeing it alone.

01:00.250 --> 01:02.330
Well, then let's go together.

01:02.330 --> 01:03.710
I wanna see it too.

01:04.130 --> 01:04.920
Huh?

01:05.330 --> 01:07.170
Uh, ah, what?!

01:07.500 --> 01:08.710
When are you going?

01:08.710 --> 01:10.170
Um, Kubo-san...

01:10.750 --> 01:12.210
I can't wait!

01:15.920 --> 01:18.710
Please, just for a moment

01:18.710 --> 01:22.750
Let the time freeze

01:24.920 --> 01:28.330
When did it start?

01:28.330 --> 01:32.000
I cannot remember

01:32.830 --> 01:36.580
Who actually cares?

01:36.580 --> 01:39.330
"It doesn't matter"

01:39.880 --> 01:42.920
Laughing or shedding tears

01:42.920 --> 01:47.080
Whenever we realized

01:47.540 --> 01:53.040
Or too persistent to take in sometime

01:54.380 --> 02:04.290
Ready? And go as the traffic light changes (As we are)

02:04.290 --> 02:08.250
No words needed (as far as we can be)

02:08.420 --> 02:11.380
we can surely make it

02:11.380 --> 02:15.040
Even if it wasn't dramatic

02:15.210 --> 02:18.880
Even if it was boring and I was moaning

02:19.170 --> 02:24.080
I'll remember this day

02:24.540 --> 02:25.540
When? I don't know

02:26.130 --> 02:29.830
I don't need no romantic words

02:30.000 --> 02:33.420
I just want one thing

02:33.500 --> 02:36.170
Let the time freeze

02:36.170 --> 02:40.080
Just for a moment...

02:40.580 --> 02:42.500
The words fell

02:46.290 --> 02:50.750
<b>Episode 11: Movie Theater and Facial Muscles</b>

02:55.710 --> 02:58.130
And now it's the day we agreed to see the movie.

02:58.960 --> 03:01.580
I've hung out with Kubo-san two times before,

03:02.960 --> 03:04.000
but I'm still not used to it.

03:09.460 --> 03:10.420
Thank you for waiting!

03:10.920 --> 03:12.210
Ah, Kubo-sa-

03:15.460 --> 03:16.130
Hm?

03:17.420 --> 03:18.580
Shiraishi-kun?

03:20.000 --> 03:21.830
The train will be here soon, so let's go.

03:22.080 --> 03:22.880
Yeah.

03:28.250 --> 03:30.920
I put my hair in a ponytail today.

03:30.920 --> 03:32.000
What do you think?

03:33.880 --> 03:34.790
It looks...

03:35.380 --> 03:36.080
Good.

03:50.040 --> 03:52.290
We made it on the train, but...

03:54.130 --> 03:55.580
There are so many people.

03:56.540 --> 03:57.380
Yeah.

03:58.830 --> 04:02.830
There should be even more people
at the next station. Will she be okay?

04:04.630 --> 04:08.210
Do you wanna use a strap? Or switch places?

04:08.380 --> 04:10.420
Thanks, but...

04:10.420 --> 04:14.580
Hmm, I'm not sure. Then you'll...

04:16.500 --> 04:18.210
Ah, that's it!

04:19.920 --> 04:21.630
Shiraishi-kun, can I

04:21.630 --> 04:23.460
hold onto your bag?

04:26.540 --> 04:28.250
That's fine.

04:36.500 --> 04:39.580
The next stop is Tachihi. Tachihi.

04:37.630 --> 04:40.580
<b>Tachihi</b>

04:37.630 --> 04:40.580
<b>Next is</b>

04:39.710 --> 04:41.920
The doors on the right side of the train will open.

04:41.170 --> 04:42.670
Still one more stop, huh?

04:41.920 --> 04:45.130
Please take care if you're near the doors.

04:45.630 --> 04:47.040
The doors will now open.

04:47.040 --> 04:47.710
Oh!

04:50.170 --> 04:51.000
Wah!

04:53.460 --> 04:54.170
Aah!

04:55.250 --> 04:57.290
Kubo-san, sorry.

05:02.040 --> 05:02.920
I'm...

05:03.460 --> 05:07.080
In such an weird position, I don't think I can move now.

05:08.380 --> 05:10.290
I'm sorry about this.

05:12.250 --> 05:14.750
The train on platform two is now departing.

05:15.170 --> 05:17.330
Please be careful of any passengers
boarding at the last moment.

05:22.000 --> 05:24.420
He's being careful not to touch me.

05:28.040 --> 05:28.880
It's okay.

05:36.420 --> 05:37.080
Argh!

05:37.380 --> 05:38.080
Ah!

05:39.040 --> 05:42.330
Is it me, or are people bumping into you pretty hard?

05:43.380 --> 05:50.420
People can't gauge how close they are to me
on crowded trains until after they bump into me.

05:51.790 --> 05:52.960
Ah, okay.

05:52.960 --> 05:55.210
But there's just one more stop.

05:55.750 --> 05:57.420
That looks super painful.

05:58.830 --> 05:59.880
Shiraishi-kun.

06:02.290 --> 06:03.630
Are you okay?

06:04.750 --> 06:05.460
Oh, I'm sor-

06:05.460 --> 06:06.630
I'm fine.

06:10.080 --> 06:13.420
Honestly, I'm not fine at all.

06:15.710 --> 06:18.500
We're finally here! How're you holding up?

06:18.500 --> 06:23.130
My legs are dying, but I'm okay.

06:23.500 --> 06:25.790
I don't remember anything after partway
through the train ride.

06:26.670 --> 06:27.580
Let's go!

06:27.580 --> 06:28.500
Yeah.

06:33.380 --> 06:35.040
Hey, look at that babe.

06:35.040 --> 06:35.750
Hmm?

06:42.540 --> 06:44.670
You're cute. You by yourself?

06:45.750 --> 06:47.830
You often see this situation in manga.

06:47.290 --> 06:49.460
You should totally get tea with us.

06:48.790 --> 06:53.000
Most of the time, a character walks up to
the heroine and says, "Did I keep you waiting?"

06:52.460 --> 06:53.670
Do you like sweets?

06:53.670 --> 06:54.460
Uh...

06:53.960 --> 06:56.330
But I'm already here.

06:55.420 --> 06:56.330
Um...

06:57.580 --> 07:01.130
Since I'm already next to her,
it'd be weird to ask, "Did I keep you waiting?"

07:01.750 --> 07:04.460
I know this killer pancake place.

07:04.460 --> 07:05.250
Um...

07:05.250 --> 07:07.210
Kubo-san is uncomfortable.

07:08.040 --> 07:09.000
Excuse me...

07:08.670 --> 07:09.500
Wah!

07:09.670 --> 07:10.920
How long have you been here?

07:10.920 --> 07:13.540
How long? Since the beginning.

07:13.540 --> 07:14.380
Liar!

07:14.630 --> 07:17.080
What, she's got a boyfriend?

07:18.420 --> 07:19.540
Are you two...

07:20.880 --> 07:21.920
Dating?

07:21.920 --> 07:22.460
Huh?

07:22.960 --> 07:24.170
Er, we're no-

07:24.170 --> 07:25.130
He's my boyfriend!

07:26.460 --> 07:27.710
Huh? Kub-

07:31.500 --> 07:32.130
Huh?

07:36.880 --> 07:39.130
What's with this bittersweet vibe?

07:41.540 --> 07:42.130
Heh.

07:42.290 --> 07:43.880
If she's got a boyfriend, then that's that!

07:43.880 --> 07:44.880
Let's bounce, boys!

07:44.880 --> 07:46.630
We're rooting for you, man!

07:46.630 --> 07:48.330
Tee-hee! So bittersweet!

07:53.580 --> 07:55.670
Should we head to the movie theater?

07:56.330 --> 07:57.040
Yeah.

07:58.880 --> 08:02.000
So I'm glad I got out of that mess,

08:03.040 --> 08:04.040
but now...

08:04.040 --> 08:05.170
Shiraishi-kun.

08:07.000 --> 08:08.710
Thanks for earlier.

08:09.580 --> 08:10.250
Huh?

08:11.630 --> 08:13.170
I felt a little scared.

08:14.710 --> 08:15.670
Oh, okay.

08:16.130 --> 08:20.290
Well, of course she was afraid
with three men surrounding her.

08:21.880 --> 08:23.540
I was scared too.

08:25.460 --> 08:27.710
Um, Kubo-san, my arm.

08:27.710 --> 08:29.000
Oh, sorry.

08:37.790 --> 08:40.170
We made it to the movie theater, but...

08:40.290 --> 08:41.500
Hmm.

08:42.790 --> 08:45.670
I'm sorry, I should've reserved us seats.

08:45.670 --> 08:48.460
I didn't think of doing that either. Sorry.

08:50.000 --> 08:52.380
The next showing is at four.

08:52.830 --> 08:55.250
We could sit next to each other at that showing.

08:56.000 --> 09:00.080
But we shouldn't stay out too late,
even if we can't sit together.

09:00.920 --> 09:02.920
Kubo-san, what seat do you want?

09:06.380 --> 09:08.460
Let's go to the four o'clock showing!

09:08.460 --> 09:11.460
Huh? But we'd get home late.

09:12.210 --> 09:16.130
That means I'd get to hang out with you longer, right?

09:18.080 --> 09:22.710
A café, an arcade, a general store, a clothing store...

09:23.330 --> 09:27.880
I wanna go loads of places
we've never been to together before.

09:29.130 --> 09:31.830
I'm sure it'll be fun.

09:34.130 --> 09:35.080
All right.

09:36.830 --> 09:39.040
We should sit beside each other
when we watch the movie too.

09:39.040 --> 09:40.750
That's the whole reason we went together.

09:41.330 --> 09:42.380
That's true.

09:42.380 --> 09:43.420
Besides...

09:44.630 --> 09:49.210
If it's late when the movie's over,
you might walk me home.

09:50.130 --> 09:51.170
Just kidding!

09:51.920 --> 09:52.670
Yeah.

09:52.670 --> 09:54.920
That was the plan.

09:54.920 --> 09:55.630
Huh?

09:59.000 --> 10:06.500
<b>Ba-dump</b>

09:59.960 --> 10:00.500
Huh?

10:00.710 --> 10:02.830
Did I say something weird?

10:05.420 --> 10:06.540
Shiraishi-kun.

10:07.330 --> 10:09.210
Wh-what?

10:10.420 --> 10:11.460
Thank you.

10:13.420 --> 10:14.130
Yeah.

10:14.830 --> 10:17.880
Then that's settled! Where should
we go until the movie starts?

10:16.080 --> 10:23.130
Admission to the 2:30 p.m. showing of Sword x Magic:
Resurrection of the Anti-Magic Dragon

10:18.420 --> 10:19.790
Anywhere's fine.

10:20.670 --> 10:23.130
That's literally the worst answer!

10:23.540 --> 10:26.880
has begun in auditorium two.

10:24.750 --> 10:25.880
Let's go to several places.

10:26.290 --> 10:28.080
We've got lots of time, after all.

10:27.540 --> 10:31.330
If you have a ticket for this showing, please go to auditorium two.

10:30.290 --> 10:31.000
Okay!

10:32.170 --> 10:35.880
Hey, how about we go to a café first? Then after that-

10:35.880 --> 10:38.670
Kubo-san, we need to pick our seats first.

10:39.000 --> 10:39.750
Oh!

10:40.040 --> 10:44.000
<b>La la!</b>

10:40.040 --> 10:44.000
<b>Phew</b>

10:40.040 --> 10:44.000
<b>She looks</b>

10:40.040 --> 10:44.000
<b>like she's</b>

10:40.040 --> 10:44.000
<b>having fun.</b>

10:47.080 --> 10:48.920
I love you, darling!

10:49.830 --> 10:51.670
I love you too, honey!

10:54.750 --> 10:56.670
So they have things like that on the menu, huh?

10:57.710 --> 10:59.080
It appears so.

10:59.830 --> 11:01.830
Shiraishi-kun, wanna order one too?

11:01.830 --> 11:04.040
Huh? Er, I'll pass.

11:04.040 --> 11:06.250
Okay then. That's too bad.

11:06.710 --> 11:08.500
I doubt you think it's too bad.

11:10.210 --> 11:12.790
Oh gosh, that was funny.

11:13.210 --> 11:16.210
They never brought you water.

11:16.580 --> 11:19.380
That's normal for me. You're getting
too much of a kick out of it.

11:21.210 --> 11:21.920
Thanks.

11:21.920 --> 11:22.830
Thank you.

11:23.250 --> 11:24.750
What're you getting, Shiraishi-kun?

11:25.580 --> 11:27.540
Hmm, let's see...

11:29.500 --> 11:30.920
Coffee sounds good.

11:31.130 --> 11:32.170
Coffee?

11:32.460 --> 11:35.330
Uh, yeah. Is something wron-

11:32.460 --> 11:35.290
<b>Japanese Coffee</b>

11:32.460 --> 11:35.290
<b>Decaf Coffee</b>

11:32.460 --> 11:35.290
<b>Espresso</b>

11:32.460 --> 11:35.290
<b>Latte</b>

11:35.540 --> 11:36.460
How grown-up!

11:37.710 --> 11:39.540
I'll also order coffee!

11:40.290 --> 11:42.710
Huh? Have you ever tried coffee before?

11:42.710 --> 11:43.380
Nope!

11:43.380 --> 11:45.290
It's Kubo-san's rarely-seen innocent side!

11:45.750 --> 11:49.880
My sister drinks coffee,
but says it can mess with your sleep.

11:49.880 --> 11:52.710
Hazuki and Tama say I'm too young to drink coffee.

11:53.000 --> 11:54.960
A-ah, okay.

11:55.330 --> 11:58.290
<b>Milk</b>

11:55.330 --> 11:58.290
<b>Oolong Tea</b>

11:55.340 --> 11:58.290
<b>Orange Juice</b>

11:55.340 --> 11:58.290
<b>Apple Juice</b>

11:55.340 --> 11:58.290
<b>Melon Soda</b>

11:55.340 --> 11:58.290
<b>Melon Soda Float</b>

11:55.340 --> 11:58.290
<b>Cola</b>

11:55.340 --> 11:58.290
<b>Hot Chocolate</b>

11:56.380 --> 11:59.670
These might be more up your alley then.

11:58.330 --> 12:00.290
<b>Oolong Tea</b>

11:58.330 --> 12:00.290
<b>Orange Juice</b>

11:58.340 --> 12:00.290
<b>Apple Juice</b>

11:58.340 --> 12:00.290
<b>Melon Soda</b>

11:58.340 --> 12:00.290
<b>Melon Soda Float</b>

12:06.790 --> 12:07.790
Hmph.

12:08.330 --> 12:11.380
If you can drink coffee, then I can too.

12:11.380 --> 12:13.080
Questionable logic and questionable confidence!

12:14.880 --> 12:16.880
Well, if that's what you want to get.

12:17.420 --> 12:20.670
Sorry, Kubo-san's friends and sister.

12:20.670 --> 12:21.580
Then it's decided!

12:24.000 --> 12:26.250
W-will this go all right?

12:29.330 --> 12:30.630
Thank you for waiting.

12:33.170 --> 12:35.420
Kubo-san looks really excited.

12:36.210 --> 12:38.170
Are you going to use sugar and creamer?

12:38.380 --> 12:39.540
I'll get some.

12:39.540 --> 12:40.960
Are you going to?

12:42.130 --> 12:44.290
I think I'll have mine black.

12:44.290 --> 12:46.380
Black! That sounds so grown-up!

12:47.040 --> 12:48.920
Then I'll have mine black too.

12:49.330 --> 12:51.130
R-really?

12:55.080 --> 12:57.210
Was this really a good idea?

13:05.040 --> 13:07.420
You can actually drink this stuff?

13:08.210 --> 13:09.210
Yeah.

13:10.920 --> 13:11.630
Oh!

13:14.500 --> 13:16.250
Yours is bitter too!

13:16.250 --> 13:17.790
We ordered the same thing!

13:18.920 --> 13:21.540
You had no problem drinking yours,

13:21.540 --> 13:26.130
so I thought maybe mine was just ridiculously bitter.

13:27.080 --> 13:29.250
I'll grab some sugar and creamer then.

13:29.250 --> 13:30.210
That's okay.

13:33.420 --> 13:35.380
We came here together,

13:36.630 --> 13:38.880
so I want to drink the same thing as you.

14:27.670 --> 14:29.250
Let's both put sugar and creamer in our coffee.

14:29.580 --> 14:32.670
But don't you like black coffee?

14:32.920 --> 14:35.250
I also drink it with sugar and creamer.

14:35.830 --> 14:40.710
I felt like drinking black coffee today,
but it's just too bitter.

14:42.670 --> 14:44.920
I think the most important thing is enjoying the taste.

14:51.290 --> 14:52.080
All right.

14:57.420 --> 15:00.000
I can drink it like this! Such a grown-up flavor!

15:00.000 --> 15:01.040
That's great.

15:03.960 --> 15:05.130
Shiraishi-kun,

15:06.170 --> 15:07.210
thanks.

15:09.460 --> 15:13.880
I can't become an adult just like that,
but it's okay to take it one step at a time, right?

15:16.210 --> 15:17.040
Yeah.

15:25.380 --> 15:26.580
So sweet.

15:39.250 --> 15:40.670
No dice again.

15:42.080 --> 15:45.080
Again? Have you done this before?

15:45.420 --> 15:47.130
Yeah. With Seita.

15:52.130 --> 15:53.380
I hope you get the one you want.

15:53.380 --> 15:53.880
Uh-huh!

16:00.170 --> 16:01.750
All right, one more time!

16:09.040 --> 16:10.790
Let's give up for today.

16:18.330 --> 16:19.750
Let me try.

16:20.130 --> 16:20.790
Huh?

16:22.210 --> 16:24.290
I'm lucky with these sorts of things.

16:29.460 --> 16:31.500
Oh! That's the one Seita wanted.

16:31.500 --> 16:34.540
Great! Then give it to Seita as a present.

16:34.670 --> 16:36.540
Er, I'd hate to take it from you.

16:36.540 --> 16:37.630
No, I'm cool with it!

16:42.790 --> 16:43.420
Ah!

16:44.000 --> 16:45.540
This one is cute!

16:45.790 --> 16:46.380
Hey!

16:47.500 --> 16:48.580
Shiraishi-kun?

16:51.040 --> 16:52.130
Are you buying that?

16:53.040 --> 16:56.830
Yeah. You can never have too many erasers.

16:57.540 --> 16:59.250
Do you have a favorite design?

16:59.670 --> 17:00.790
Nah, not really.

17:01.170 --> 17:02.330
Whatever is fine.

17:02.750 --> 17:04.250
Hmm.

17:04.250 --> 17:07.330
Oh, then you should get this one.

17:07.960 --> 17:08.630
Ah...

17:09.500 --> 17:10.750
Huh, this one?

17:10.830 --> 17:13.210
But you said whatever is fine, right?

17:13.210 --> 17:14.210
What?!

17:28.210 --> 17:28.790
No way!

17:29.330 --> 17:32.460
Yikes! Shiraishi-kun, if we don't hurry,
we'll miss the movie!

17:37.080 --> 17:39.290
The movie theater's atmosphere is so nice, isn't it?

17:39.630 --> 17:41.670
Yeah, it's relaxing.

17:42.040 --> 17:44.920
If I stay up all night, will I fall asleep quickly?

17:44.210 --> 17:45.210
Phew.

17:44.920 --> 17:46.420
No, watch the movie.

17:45.710 --> 17:47.580
We made it just in the nick of time.

17:48.080 --> 17:49.580
Isn't this where you sleep?

17:48.080 --> 17:52.540
<b>Fidget</b>

17:48.330 --> 17:49.000
Yep.

17:49.130 --> 17:51.460
Shiraishi-kun's fidgeting!

17:59.580 --> 18:05.330
This is a story of nameless hero living
in a world with swords and magic...

18:06.290 --> 18:10.710
Sword x Magic: Resurrection of the Anti-Magic Dragon.

18:11.920 --> 18:14.250
Aww, I'm starving!

18:14.250 --> 18:17.000
We've almost reached town, so hang in there.

18:17.000 --> 18:20.210
I'm sick of hearing stuff like that!

18:20.710 --> 18:22.750
This kid's a real wimp, huh?

18:22.750 --> 18:24.750
We should ditch wimps.

18:24.750 --> 18:26.250
How heartless!

18:26.380 --> 18:28.250
You cruel, callous duo!

18:28.250 --> 18:29.750
What'd ya say?

18:29.750 --> 18:32.630
Who do you think guided us here?

18:32.630 --> 18:34.130
I'm so famished, I can't move!

18:33.330 --> 18:34.040
Oh!

18:34.130 --> 18:36.170
I can see the town! Zaasan!

18:36.170 --> 18:36.880
Huh?

18:41.790 --> 18:45.750
<b>Goodbye</b>

18:41.790 --> 18:45.750
<b>vocabulary</b>

18:42.670 --> 18:43.460
Incredible!

18:43.670 --> 18:45.210
I'm glad we came to see it!

18:47.420 --> 18:48.170
Kubo-san?

18:49.170 --> 18:52.460
It's nice to share an interest, isn't it?

18:54.580 --> 18:55.460
Yeah, it is.

18:56.710 --> 18:58.460
Shiraishi-kun, did you notice?

18:58.460 --> 18:59.380
Notice what?

19:00.330 --> 19:04.540
Your facial expression changed a lot
when you watched the movie.

19:04.540 --> 19:05.210
Huh?

19:05.210 --> 19:07.710
Your expression normally doesn't change much.

19:07.710 --> 19:09.790
I thought it was out of the ordinary.

19:12.130 --> 19:13.130
That's because...

19:15.330 --> 19:20.710
It's eerie to smile to yourself and stuff
when you're in places like a classroom.

19:21.080 --> 19:22.920
Ah. So that's why.

19:23.420 --> 19:24.130
Yep.

19:24.880 --> 19:27.420
People rarely strike up conversations with me as it is,

19:27.420 --> 19:32.080
so if they do spot me and catch me smiling at nothing,
they'll be even less likely to talk to me.

19:32.460 --> 19:36.040
You don't need to worry about that
when you're with me though.

19:41.920 --> 19:44.330
Hey now, we're going home.

19:46.290 --> 19:50.880
It's something I've been careful about since elementary
school, and I can't change it with a snap of my fingers.

19:51.170 --> 19:52.420
That makes sense.

19:52.960 --> 19:57.500
Well, even if you don't show your feelings
on your face, you're pretty easy to read.

19:57.500 --> 19:59.210
If that's true, that's a proble-

19:59.210 --> 20:01.960
Hmm? Did you say something just now?

20:02.250 --> 20:03.540
No, it was nothing.

20:04.040 --> 20:04.920
Let's go home.

20:04.920 --> 20:07.130
Hm? Okay.

20:30.210 --> 20:31.880
Thanks for walking me home.

20:32.170 --> 20:33.710
Oh, yeah.

20:34.710 --> 20:37.290
Shiraishi-kun, make it home safe.

20:37.290 --> 20:38.290
All right.

20:41.960 --> 20:42.750
Hey.

20:43.000 --> 20:45.380
What'd you think of today?

20:46.210 --> 20:47.420
What'd I think?

20:47.420 --> 20:48.460
Did you have fun?

20:50.580 --> 20:52.710
Yeah. It was fun.

20:54.130 --> 20:55.960
Where shall we go next time?

20:56.330 --> 20:57.130
Huh?

20:58.170 --> 21:01.210
I had a lot of fun today too.

21:02.210 --> 21:05.960
So I want to hang out with you again.

21:08.290 --> 21:10.040
If you wanna.

21:10.040 --> 21:11.000
Really?

21:12.170 --> 21:13.250
It's a promise, okay?

21:16.420 --> 21:17.210
Okay.

21:21.580 --> 21:23.000
See you at school!

21:23.250 --> 21:24.000
Yeah.

21:28.000 --> 21:33.750
According to Kubo-san, my facial muscles
were more active than usual today.

21:35.290 --> 21:40.210
And she said I'm pretty easy to read even
if I don't show anything on my face.

21:44.000 --> 21:46.710
How easy is "pretty easy to read?"

21:48.580 --> 21:49.710
For instance, that time.

21:50.380 --> 21:51.540
Or that time.

21:53.580 --> 21:54.830
Or that time.

21:55.130 --> 21:56.330
Or that time.

21:58.080 --> 21:59.330
Or just earlier.

22:02.000 --> 22:04.630
I didn't let anything show, right?

22:11.170 --> 22:14.540
The school's shadow glows a dark red

22:14.540 --> 22:20.830
I haven't reached the end of my youth

22:21.080 --> 22:26.250
I've experienced a little bit of it, but it'll be over soon

22:26.250 --> 22:30.500
Along with the smiles you give me

22:30.500 --> 22:32.420
It's beautiful

22:32.420 --> 22:35.250
Is it okay to call this a miracle?

22:35.500 --> 22:41.170
I love, love, love these days

22:41.170 --> 22:47.630
But they won't last forever, so I tightly hold on to them

22:47.630 --> 22:51.750
Because we're kids and our spring has just begun

22:51.750 --> 22:55.130
Let's move forward, forward forward, one step at a time

22:55.130 --> 22:58.460
Now, a firm wind faintly blows

22:58.460 --> 23:06.130
I hope our time together at least colors the world a little

23:06.130 --> 23:10.750
What kind of canvas will we paint? What kind of future will we have?

23:10.750 --> 23:14.540
I don't know, but I want to believe

23:13.830 --> 23:18.130
We'll definitely smile and wave at each other

23:14.920 --> 23:17.960
We look forward to tomorrow a little

23:17.960 --> 23:21.670
When we say, "See you later" to each other

23:21.750 --> 23:28.630
With the season's quick passing, our words repeat

23:28.630 --> 23:35.040
Please, please may we be happy!
